  "text": "```verilog\nmodule apbslave #(\n\t\tparameter\tC_APB_ADDR_WIDTH = 12,\n\t\tparameter\tC_APB_DATA_WIDTH = 32,\n\t\tlocalparam\tAW = C_APB_ADDR_WIDTH,\n\t\tlocalparam\tDW = C_APB_DATA_WIDTH,\n\t\tlocalparam\tAPBLSB = $clog2(C_APB_DATA_WIDTH)-3\n\t) (\n\t\tinput\twire\t\t\tPCLK, PRESETn,\n\t\tinput\twire\t\t\tPSEL,\n\t\tinput\twire\t\t\tPENABLE,\n\t\toutput\treg\t\t\tPREADY,\n\t\tinput\twire\t[AW-1:0]\tPADDR,\n\t\tinput\twire\t\t\tPWRITE,\n\t\tinput\twire\t[DW-1:0]\tPWDATA,\n\t\tinput\twire\t[DW/8-1:0]\tPWSTRB,\n\t\tinput\twire\t[2:0]\t\tPPROT,\n\t\toutput\treg\t[DW-1:0]\tPRDATA,\n\t\toutput\twire\t\t\tPSLVERR\n\t);\n\n\t// Internal register file\n\treg [DW-1:0] mem [0:2**AW-1];\n\n\t// APB state machine\n\tlocalparam S_IDLE = 1'b0;\n\tlocalparam S_SETUP = 1'b1;\n\tlocalparam S_ACCESS = 1'b1; // Simplified: use PENABLE to distinguish\n\n\t// We'll use a simple approach:\n\t// PREADY is high when not in access phase\n\t// During setup phase (PSEL=1, PENABLE=0), PREADY can be high or low\n\t// During access phase (PSEL=1, PENABLE=1), PREADY indicates completion\n\n\t// For a simple slave, we can complete in one cycle:\n\t// PREADY is always high when PSEL is high, meaning the slave is ready\n\t// This is the simplest valid APB slave behavior\n\n\t// Let's implement a proper APB slave with a register file\n\t// The address is used to index into the register file\n\t// We'll use the upper bits of the address as the register index\n\n\t// Calculate the register index from the address\n\twire [AW-APBLSB-1:0] reg_index = PADDR[AW-1:APBLSB];\n\n\t// Write enable: during access phase, write operation\n\twire write_en = PSEL & PENABLE & PWRITE;\n\n\t// Read data: from the register file\n\tassign PRDATA = mem[reg_index];\n\n\t// PREADY: high when the slave is ready to complete the transfer\n\t// For a simple slave, we can assert PREADY in the access phase\n\t// This means the transfer completes in one cycle\n\tassign PREADY = PSEL;\n\n\t// PSLVERR: always low for in-range accesses\n\tassign PSLVERR = 1'b0;\n\n\t// Write to register file\n\talways @(posedge PCLK or negedge PRESETn) begin\n\t\tif (!PRESETn) begin\n\t\t\t// Reset: clear all registers (optional, but good practice)\n\t\t\t// For simplicity, we'll just let them be uninitialized\n\t\t\t// In a real design, you might want to initialize them\n\t\tend else if (write_en) begin\n\t\t\t// Write with byte strobes\n\t\t\tinteger i;\n\t\t\tfor (i = 0; i < DW/8; i = i + 1) begin\n\t\t\t\tif (PWSTRB[i]) begin\n\t\t\t\t\tmem[reg_index][i*8 +: 8] <= PWDATA[i*8 +: 8];\n\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\tend\n\t\tend\n\tend\n\n\t// Initialize PREADY and PRDATA\n\talways @(posedge PCLK or negedge PRESETn) begin\n\t\tif (!PRESETn) begin\n\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b0;\n\t\t\tPRDATA <= {DW{1'b0}};\n\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\tPREADY <= PSEL;\n\t\t\tPRDATA <= mem[reg_index];\n\t\tend\n\tend\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>",
